  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree (connected, undirected, acyclic graph) consisting of NNN nodes. Based on this tree, you have to answer QQQ queries.\n\nEach query is of the form:\n\n\nK&nbsp;D&nbsp;V1&nbsp;V2&nbsp;⋯&nbsp;VKK\\ D\\  V_1\\ V_2\\ \\cdots\\ V_KK&nbsp;D&nbsp;V1​&nbsp;V2​&nbsp;⋯&nbsp;VK​ - output the number of pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j), 1≤i&lt;j≤K1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq K1≤i&lt;j≤K, such that the shortest path between nodes ViV_iVi​ and VjV_jVj​ in the tree has DDD edges.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\leq T \\leq 51≤T≤5",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\leq N, Q \\leq 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "1≤u,v,Vi≤N1 \\leq u, v, V_i \\leq N1≤u,v,Vi​≤N",
      "0≤D≤1050 \\leq D \\leq 10^50≤D≤105",
      "The sum of KKK across all queries in a single test case is at most 10510^5105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (20 points):** For each query, K≤10K \\leq 10K≤10",
      "**Subtask 2 (80 points):** Original constraints",
      "Sample Input`1",
      "5 2",
      "1 2",
      "1 3",
      "2 4",
      "4 5",
      "3 2 2 3 5",
      "2 4 1 3",
      "`Sample Output`2",
      "0",
      "`ExplanationIn the first query, the pairs of nodes (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3) and (2,5)(2, 5)(2,5) have distance 222.",
      "In the second query, there is no pair with distance 444."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line contains an integer TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers, NNN and QQQ.\nN−1N - 1N−1 lines follow. Each line consists of two integers uuu and vvv, indicating that there is an edge between nodes uuu and vvv in the tree.\nQQQ lines follow. Each line describes a query in the format given above.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, output the answer on a new line.",
